challenges.description:
What is the return type of this function?

  async function getName(): Promise<string> {
    return "Alice"
  }

If you call `getName()` without await, what do you get?

Given:

  async function getCount(): Promise<number> {
    return 42
  }

  async function main() {
    const count = await getCount()
    // what type is count here?
  }

What type does TypeScript infer for `count`?

What type does TypeScript give `err` in a catch block?

  try {
    await riskyOperation()
  } catch (err) {
    // what is the type of err?
  }

What is the correct way to pass cancellation signal to a fetch call?

  const controller = new AbortController()

  // cancel after 5 seconds
  setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000)

  // which option correctly passes the signal?

  A)  fetch(url, { abort: controller })
  B)  fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal })
  C)  fetch(url, { controller: controller.signal })
  D)  fetch(url).abort(controller.signal)

What does this function produce?

  async function* streamLines(text: string): AsyncGenerator<string> {
    for (const line of text.split('\n')) {
      yield line
    }
  }

  // consumed with:
  for await (const line of streamLines("a\nb\nc")) {
    console.log(line)
  }
